<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarre (department)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1814</span> · Also known as Saar department</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarre was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of the French Republic and Empire on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, created in 1798 from occupied German lands, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>. It covered the Saar, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunsruck">Hunsrück</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> valley. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s defeat in 1814 its lands were divided, mostly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, with smaller parts going to Oldenburg and other German states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarre-department.jpg" alt="Sarre (department)" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Excommunicato (original version by Naturals) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarre_departement_(1812).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
